      "He ordered hand washing in chlorinated lime. Deaths in the first clinic fell from eighteen per cent to about two. He could not say why it worked.",
      "Other doctors rejected him. Washing hands meant doctors carried death between beds. Senior physicians took that as an insult. His contract was not renewed.",
      "Semmelweis died in an asylum in 1865. Lister published on antiseptic surgery two years later. Pasteur soon gave the explanation.",
